MongoDB is useful for HR systems with flexible employee records, where different employees may have different information.



MongoDB is suitable for storing resumes, skills, project details, and frequently changing employee data.



PostgreSQL is better for structured HR data such as employee details, salaries, attendance, and payroll.



PostgreSQL provides strong relationships, transactions, and constraints to maintain accurate and consistent data.



I would choose MongoDB for flexible data and PostgreSQL for structured data and reliable transactions in an HR system.